.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:1:# ISSUE-023 — Refine goal dependency triggers and external watchers
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:7:Next best session: design refinement pass for wait-condition watchers
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:8:Next best session rationale: Watcher types, execution safety, persistence, and stale-guard behavior need design locking.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:11:Depends on: `.ai/issues/open/ISSUE-016-goal-idle-tolerant-mode.md`
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:13:Goal: Design optional external dependency triggers so an idle-tolerant goal can resume when a watched command, file, process, or agent signal changes.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:17:Idle-tolerant goals allow an agent to wait, but a time-based nudge alone may be inefficient. Some waits have concrete external conditions: a command exits, a log contains a string, a file appears, a test server becomes reachable, or another agent posts a completion signal.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:25:  - process/session signal arrives.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:26:- When a condition is satisfied, `pi-goal` nudges or resumes the goal if it is still active and waiting.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:27:- Watchers are visible, cancelable, stale-guarded by goal id, and timeout-limited.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:31:1. Which watcher types are safe for a first version?
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:32:2. Are watchers executed by the extension, the agent, or an external helper CLI?
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:34:4. How are watcher registrations persisted and restored after reload?
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:35:5. How does this interact with worktrees and multiple parallel goals?
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:40:- Watcher satisfaction triggers at most one stale-guarded nudge/resume event per registration.
.ai/issues/refine/ISSUE-023-goal-dependency-triggers-and-watchers.md:41:- User can list/cancel active wait conditions.
